ServiceLoader on the linear-memory wasm target corrupted the heap: ServiceLoadWasmRuntime.createServices allocated
its result with Allocator.allocateArray(cls, n), where cls is the SERVICE class, not its array class. allocateArray
takes the array class (it reads the component type through tag.itemType, null for a non-array class), so the result
got the service interface's header and a wrong size, and storing the service objects wrote past it: the next
object's header became the array length (1) and the GC's region walk later never ended. Found by walking the heap
every allocation (mctick, java.nio.file.spi.FileSystemProvider.installedProviders from Minecraft's Util.<clinit>).
Now the array class (cls.arrayType), as everywhere else.
Codegen: this runtime method only.

diff --git a/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/ServiceLoadWasmRuntime.java b/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/ServiceLoadWasmRuntime.java
index fa2adbd3b..e487c19a0 100644
--- a/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/ServiceLoadWasmRuntime.java
+++ b/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/impl/ServiceLoadWasmRuntime.java
@@ -37,7 +37,11 @@ final class ServiceLoadWasmRuntime {
         entry = entry.add(Address.sizeOf()).getAddress();
         var size = entry.getInt();
         entry = entry.add(4);
-        RuntimeArray result = Allocator.allocateArray(cls, size).toStructure();
+        // wjharness patch 0008: allocateArray takes the ARRAY class; cls is the service class. Object[] when the
+        // service's own array class was not generated (the caller treats the result as Object[] anyway).
+        RuntimeClass arrayClass = cls.arrayType != null ? cls.arrayType
+                : RuntimeClass.getClass(Address.ofObject(new Object[0]).toStructure());
+        RuntimeArray result = Allocator.allocateArray(arrayClass, size).toStructure();
         var resultData = WasmRuntime.align(result.toAddress().add(Structure.sizeOf(RuntimeArray.class)),
                 Address.sizeOf());
         for (var i = 0; i < size; ++i) {
